# tools/cr/crypto_monocypher_hchacha20_parity_witness.rish -- Monocypher-source parity for the standalone HChaCha20 (crypto_chacha20_h) subkey-derivation
# core, the nonce-extension the whole XChaCha line folds through -- the 256-bit subkey every random-nonce sealed message (Vault, Comlink, the Lotus
# signed carry) derives before enciphering. Our authored crypto/xchacha20.rye's hchacha20 and the vendored Monocypher's own C (vendor/monocypher,
# CC0/BSD-dual), each compiled fresh and asked for the same six subkeys, diffed byte-for-byte. The TWELFTH rung of the real Monocypher-source parity
# pattern (BLAKE2b - X25519 - Ed25519 - IETF AEAD - Argon2 - XChaCha20-Poly1305 flagship - Edwards<->Montgomery - standalone Poly1305 - standalone
# ChaCha20 - standalone SHA-512 - HMAC-SHA-512 came before). Season G - Cryptography.
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season G thread (Cryptography - Rye-native, Monocypher-parity, audit-ready).
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md -- Season G's crux rungs name "the parity witness
# proving Rye output equals Monocypher output byte-for-byte." crypto/xchacha20.rye proved HChaCha20 against the draft §2.2.1 known-answer and inside
# the AEAD flagship, yet never STANDALONE against Monocypher's own crypto_chacha20_h -- so the subkey-derivation core the whole XChaCha nonce-extension
# rests on now stands proven in its own right, the nonce-extension counterpart to the standalone ChaCha20 and Poly1305 rungs that prove the AEAD's other halves.
# Kin: crypto/xchacha20.rye (our authored HChaCha20 + XChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD, GREEN against Zig's std.crypto and the draft vector) - tools/rye/monocypher_hchacha20_parity.rye
# (our printing harness) - tools/fixtures/monocypher_hchacha20_harness.c (Monocypher's printing harness) - tools/cr/crypto_monocypher_chacha20_parity_witness.rish
# (the standalone ChaCha20 sibling -- together they prove the XChaCha construction's cores standalone). Monocypher stays the parity TARGET, vendored and
# unmodified, never a copied line, studied clean-room (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# The six lines are anchored to the world: line 1 is the draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03 §2.2.1 published HChaCha20 subkey (the canonical known-answer,
# 82413b42...d3ecdc); lines 2-6 are subkeys over deterministic (key, input) pairs, where the oracle is a second real implementation agreeing byte-for-byte.
# Purely local -- no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the Season's named horizon.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cr/crypto_monocypher_hchacha20_parity_witness.rish

say "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: Language EN — Monocypher-source parity for the standalone HChaCha20 (crypto_chacha20_h) subkey-derivation core, the nonce-extension the whole XChaCha line folds through. crypto/xchacha20.rye proved HChaCha20 against the draft §2.2.1 known-answer and inside the AEAD flagship yet never STANDALONE against Monocypher's own crypto_chacha20_h; this twelfth rung closes it, proving the core STANDALONE against the ACTUAL vendored Monocypher C over six subkeys, byte-for-byte."
say "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: Style Radiant — like against like. Our authored HChaCha20 and the unmodified vendored Monocypher each compile fresh and each print, in order, the draft §2.2.1 published subkey then HChaCha20 subkeys over five deterministic (key, input) pairs. Two independent implementations, one set of inputs; the parity is that the six subkeys agree hex for hex."
say "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: Lens TAME — no fabricated constant is trusted: line 1 is anchored to the draft §2.2.1 published subkey 82413b42…d3ecdc; the remaining lines' oracle is a second real implementation. The witness diffs the six Monocypher lines against the six Rye lines byte-for-byte AND asserts the published anchor. Monocypher is linked, never copied. Purely local — no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let cbin = "crypto/bin/monocypher_hchacha20"
let cout = "crypto/bin/monocypher_hchacha20.out"
let rout = "crypto/bin/rye_hchacha20.out"

# 1. Build the Monocypher C harness, linking the unmodified vendored source with zig cc.
let cbuild = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && ${zig} cc -O2 -I vendor/monocypher/src tools/fixtures/monocypher_hchacha20_harness.c vendor/monocypher/src/monocypher.c -o ${cbin}"]
assert cbuild.ok else "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: Monocypher C harness build failed — ${cbuild.err}"

# 2. Run the Monocypher C harness -- six subkey hex lines.
let crun = run ["sh" "-c" "${cbin} > ${cout} 2>&1"]
assert crun.ok else "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: Monocypher C harness exited non-zero — see ${cout}"

# 3. Run our authored Rye harness -- six subkey hex lines over the identical inputs.
let rrun = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye run tools/rye/monocypher_hchacha20_parity.rye > ${rout} 2>&1"]
assert rrun.ok else "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: Rye harness exited non-zero — see ${rout}"

# 4. Byte-for-byte parity: the two six-line outputs must be identical.
let diff = run ["sh" "-c" "diff ${cout} ${rout} > /dev/null && echo same"]
assert (trim diff.out) == "same" else "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: Monocypher and Rye subkeys disagree — Monocypher:\n$(cat ${cout})\nRye:\n$(cat ${rout})"

# 5. Anchor to the world: line 1 is the draft §2.2.1 published HChaCha20 subkey.
let draft_subkey = "82413b4227b27bfed30e42508a877d73a0f9e4d58a74a853c12ec41326d3ecdc"

let got_subkey = run ["sh" "-c" "sed -n '1p' ${cout}"]
assert (trim got_subkey.out) == draft_subkey else "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: line 1 is not the draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03 §2.2.1 published HChaCha20 subkey"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${cout}"]
say "crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: the six subkeys, agreed by both implementations:\n${shown.out}"

say "GREEN crypto-monocypher-hchacha20-parity: our authored crypto/xchacha20.rye's hchacha20 and the vendored Monocypher's own C (crypto_chacha20_h), each compiled fresh, produce byte-for-byte identical HChaCha20 subkeys over the draft §2.2.1 published known-answer (anchored to 82413b42…d3ecdc) and five deterministic (key, input) pairs. The TWELFTH real Monocypher-SOURCE parity rung, proving the subkey-derivation core every random-nonce sealed message (Vault, Comlink, the Lotus signed carry) folds through in its own right — the nonce-extension counterpart to the standalone ChaCha20 and Poly1305 rungs that prove the AEAD's other halves. Monocypher stays vendored and unmodified, linked never copied. Purely local, no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."
